      "content": "That's a great start, thank you. One thing though—I feel like the part about the meetings is a little too \"HR-speak\" and might come across as a bit cold to them since they are such a high performer. Is there a way to phrase the criticism about their punctuality so it sounds a bit more \"human\" or \"personality-driven\" without losing the professional edge? Like, maybe acknowledging that they have a unique way of managing their time or something?",
